    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "The line $y=3x+6$ crosses the $x$-axis at an angle of $\\theta$ with the positive direction of the $x$-axis. Find the value of $\\theta$, correct to 1 decimal place.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=71.6^\\circ$\n\nThe gradient equals $\\tan\\theta$.",
      "worked": "The gradient of $y=3x+6$ is $3$. Since gradient is rise divided by run, it equals $\\tan\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=3\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}3\\\\\\theta&\\approx71.6^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
